# Config for `npm run tools:dev` / `tools:build`.
# Copy to `src/tools/.env` (git-ignored) and fill in. Vite only exposes VITE_* vars,
# and reads this file from THIS directory — src/web/.env does not apply here.
# Restart the dev server after changing it.

# Magiloom server origin. Omit to use the built-in default
# (wss://magiserver.up.railway.app) — which is usually what you want, since the tools
# site talks to the real server even in development. For a LOCAL server:
# VITE_MAGILOOM_SERVER=ws://localhost:8787

# NOTE: the tools site needs no gateway token. It only calls the REST endpoints
# (/auth, /logs) with the account's own bearer token — it never opens the game
# WebSocket, so MAGILOOM_TOKEN isn't involved.

# If sign-in fails here with "Could not reach the Magiloom server" while the server
# is plainly up, it's almost certainly CORS: the server's MAGILOOM_ALLOW_ORIGIN must
# list this dev origin (http://localhost:5181) as well as the deployed site.
